# asr-wav2vec_ctc-300m-amh-3273h-v1.0

amharic-ctc-300m v0.3 (2026-11-12) is the small sibling of amharic-ctc v0.3 (1B): Meta's omniASR_CTC_300M_v2
(24 layers, 326M parameters, a third of the 1B) with a LoRA fine-tune merged in, trained with exactly the v0.3 recipe
and data (0.78 h of human-corrected Amilia, manifest v2026-11-04, + snapwre read speech 1:1, letter variants merged).
It is a separate model line for CPU-only and live-dictation use on weak machines; it does **not** replace the 1B
(the two families remain separate). Same API, files and tokenizer as the 1B bundle: swap the folder.

## Variants

- `asr-wav2vec_ctc-300m-amh-fp16`: PyTorch inference with FP16-stored weights, approximately 0.65 GB.
- `asr-wav2vec_ctc-300m-amh-int8_onnx`: ONNX Runtime CPU inference without PyTorch, approximately 0.37 GB.

Use the repository manifest for the exact file inventory, byte sizes and checksums.

## What to expect

Character error rate (letter variants merged, punctuation removed), greedy decoding:

| set | 300M v0.3 | 1B v0.3 | 300M base |
|---|---|---|---|
| Amilia test (conversational, 50 clips) | 21.8 | 15.9 | 47.0 |
| WAXAL (100) | 16.4 | 13.0 | 17.1 |
| snapwre read speech (200) | 14.9 | 10.4 | 16.5 |
| leyu phone speech (200) | 16.0 | 11.3 | 16.6 |
| Amilia heldout1104 (75) | 24.7 | 16.9 | 45.5 |

About 6 CER points worse than the 1B on conversation (word error rate 56% vs 42%): fine for a draft or live
captions on a weak CPU, but use the 1B for transcripts that will be kept. Output style is the same (Ge'ez as spoken,
`።` `፣` `?`, numbers as words, common letter of each variant group). Keep `model_version` ("v0.3") and the model
name (`amharic-ctc-300m`) with every transcript: the two models are different ASR models.

## Use

As for the 1B: `CTCTranscriber("<bundle>/model")`, `StreamingTranscriber` (see STREAMING.md), or for the ONNX
variant `asr_onnx_infer.OnnxCTCTranscriber("<variant folder>")`.
